<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:11:14 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>The Observers</category><title>Hate speech against Rohingya refugees on the rise in Malaysia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260911-hate-speech-rohingya-refugees-rise-malaysia</link><description>
Hostile social media content, disinformation campaigns, and a petition calling for their expulsion: in Malaysia, a wave of hate speech has been targeting Rohingya refugees, a Muslim minority driven out of Myanmar. The rising hostility has already led to the eviction of more than 100 people from a village and forced the temporary closure of schools serving refugee children.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78029d66-adea-11f1-ab9f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Unbenannt-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78029d66-adea-11f1-ab9f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Unbenannt-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">775b02f2-ad38-11f1-8f3b-e32b0cda81f5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:34:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>Nepal: Rescue efforts continue in the aftermath of a flash flooding disaster</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260911-nepal-rescue-efforts-continue-in-the-aftermath-of-a-flash-flooding-disaster</link><description>
Two weeks after the devastating flash floods, the number of dead and missing continues to rise. At Kathmandu’s public hospital, as well as outside the military base in Bidur, hundreds of photographs of missing people have been put up. Hundreds of families come forward, hoping for news – good or bad – of one or more loved ones. A race against time is underway: helping survivors, finding those still alive and identifying the victims. Rescue teams have been carrying out repeated helicopter flights, as air access is now the only way to reach remote areas cut off from the rest of the world. Civil society has also mobilised, particularly Nepal’s Generation Z. From Kathmandu to Betrawati, FRANCE 24's reporters Alban Alvarez and Fantine Dantzer accompanied a humanitarian convoy along one of the country’s most treacherous roads.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9842b8cc-adc2-11f1-b741-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/reporters-11-9-2026.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9842b8cc-adc2-11f1-b741-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/reporters-11-9-2026.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdd519d4-adc3-11f1-8bfe-bd17830f66bc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:41:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Alban ALVAREZ</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Putin arrives in India for BRICS summit set to be dominated by Middle East, Ukraine wars</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-putin-xi-india-brics-summit-ukraine-middle-east-wars</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin arrived in New Delhi on Friday for a two-day BRICS summit expected to focus on wars in Ukraine and the Middle East and economic challenges. Putin and Iran’s President Masoud Pezeshkian are due to meet Prime Minister Narendra Modi, while China’s Xi Jinping is also expected to hold talks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0d61468-acf3-11f1-ab71-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/7e5fcf827b46397639dc014e8f6942451ecb7847.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0d61468-acf3-11f1-ab71-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/7e5fcf827b46397639dc014e8f6942451ecb7847.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d205e28a-ad83-11f1-a855-07ef7956a524</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 02:08:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0d61468-acf3-11f1-ab71-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/7e5fcf827b46397639dc014e8f6942451ecb7847.jpg">© Sajjad Hussain, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Hong Kong court sentences Tiananmen vigil activists to between 5 and 7 years in jail</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-hong-kong-court-sentences-tiananmen-vigil-activists-to-between-5-and-7-years-in-jail</link><description>
Three activists who had held annual vigils commemorating the Tiananmen Square crackdown were sentenced to between five and seven years in prison Friday for calling for an "end to one-party dictatorship". Prosecutors had argued that China's constitution enshrines the primacy of the Communist Party.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a6cd0a-ad92-11f1-b92e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a1ca4390fa1cddd8c8e78e0df94a508efc1e3ec4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a6cd0a-ad92-11f1-b92e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a1ca4390fa1cddd8c8e78e0df94a508efc1e3ec4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0042bb60-ad83-11f1-8e0c-07ef7956a524</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:49:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a6cd0a-ad92-11f1-b92e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a1ca4390fa1cddd8c8e78e0df94a508efc1e3ec4.jpg">© Isaac Lawrence, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Seoul spy agency unveils potential new heir to North Korea’s Kim Jong-un</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260910-north-korea-succession-in-question-as-seoul-spy-agency-unveils-potential-new-heir</link><description>
A South Korean spy agency on Thursday revealed that North Korean leader Kim Jong-un could have a child born before his chosen successor, daughter Kim Ju Ae, which raises questions about succession. Information about the Kim dynasty is scarce and often difficult to verify. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00780202-acf7-11f1-9b27-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/b308b3b6cd604467ae2cde95a9654e2d57b55da7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00780202-acf7-11f1-9b27-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/b308b3b6cd604467ae2cde95a9654e2d57b55da7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01a4f374-acf7-11f1-9153-bfbc394ea958</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 09:07:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00780202-acf7-11f1-9b27-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/b308b3b6cd604467ae2cde95a9654e2d57b55da7.jpg">© Korean Central News Agency (KCNA) via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Deadly Philippines ferry fire leaves dozens missing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260910-at-least-five-killed-87-missing-after-ferry-fire-in-philippines</link><description>
At least five people died and dozens were unaccounted for Thursday after a ferry caught fire off the Philippine island province of Palawan, with 43 passengers and crew rescued so far. Coast guard teams continued search and rescue operations as officials worked to establish what happened.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de697182-acb0-11f1-848c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7UR9VL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de697182-acb0-11f1-848c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7UR9VL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60942422-acb6-11f1-ab5e-9924198a0345</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:24:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de697182-acb0-11f1-848c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7UR9VL.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>The world's third global aerospace market: India's civil aviation sector takes off</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260909-the-world-s-third-global-aerospace-market-india-s-civil-aviation-sector-takes-off</link><description>
The aviation sector is one of the India's strongest-performing industries. More than 70 airports have been built over the past decade, and the country counts over 400 million air passengers annually. In just ten years, India has become the world's third-largest aviation market, behind China and the United States.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/555d26d8-ab9b-11f1-b5bd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/V1-FR-F24-FOCUS-INDIA-CIVIL-AVIATION-29062026-FF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/555d26d8-ab9b-11f1-b5bd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/V1-FR-F24-FOCUS-INDIA-CIVIL-AVIATION-29062026-FF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">754eda76-ab9c-11f1-b892-d5d37e7d97b0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 12:34:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Alban ALVAREZ</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spoiler alert: AI in cinema 'just a tool, won’t replace actors and human beings'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-spoiler-alert-ai-in-cinema-just-a-tool-won-t-replace-actors-and-human-beings-1</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome film producer Lahoucine Grimich. He challenges the prevailing narrative that cinema is an industry in existential crisis. While acknowledging that viewing habits have dramatically shifted since the pandemic, he argues that streaming platforms, public support and theatrical exhibition are not competing forces. As demonstrated in the French model, they form parts of an interconnected financing ecosystem in which cinema can adapt without ever abandoning the big screen. He frames filmmaking as a form of cultural sovereignty: societies need films not simply as entertainment, but to recognise themselves and to create what he calls “new imaginaries.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ffeb164-ab86-11f1-8ddf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-081209-081733-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ffeb164-ab86-11f1-8ddf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260908-081209-081733-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">37cce99c-ab86-11f1-9bb5-637ae701f8ef</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:11:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Nepal rescuers race to free dozens trapped in hydropower tunnels</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260908-nepal-rescuers-race-to-free-dozens-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnels</link><description>
Authorities in Nepal on Tuesday said that rescuers are focusing on three hydropower project tunnels where they believe dozens of workers could be trapped. The announcement came two weeks after ​a devastating ‌flood killed that hundreds and left thousands missing in the Himalayan country and in ⁠neighbouring China's Tibet region.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/187d0ac8-ab4e-11f1-a8f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7HW2ZT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/187d0ac8-ab4e-11f1-a8f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7HW2ZT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4cbfcc0-ab4f-11f1-b918-29caed3e7682</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 06:51:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/187d0ac8-ab4e-11f1-a8f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7HW2ZT.jpg">© Pedro Pardo, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Eight airports in Indonesia suspend operations after volcanic eruption</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260906-six-airports-in-indonesia-suspend-operations-after-volcanic-eruption</link><description>
Eight airports in Indonesia, including Jakarta's main international airport, suspended operations Sunday after the erupting Anak Krakatoa volcano spewed clouds of ash across the archipelago. Geologists said that the latest series of eruptions does not have the potential to trigger a tsunami at this time.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7973d472-a9c0-11f1-a0ea-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/7a7569133a3d2c491f8f59c7f29eff6f7bc0b4e0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7973d472-a9c0-11f1-a0ea-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/7a7569133a3d2c491f8f59c7f29eff6f7bc0b4e0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7ac58c12-a9c0-11f1-8628-b7773d79cef0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 06:59:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7973d472-a9c0-11f1-a0ea-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/7a7569133a3d2c491f8f59c7f29eff6f7bc0b4e0.jpg">© Ronald Siagian, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>'I don't know if I'm dreaming': Rebuilding lives after Nepal's devastating floods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260905-i-dont-know-if-im-dreaming-rebuilding-lives-after-nepal-devastating-floods</link><description>
With thousands of people driven from their homes by a massive flash flood that swept entire villages away, FRANCE 24 visits a school in Nepal's remote Rasuwa district that has been converted to a temporary shelter for the dispossessed. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d75e6228-a907-11f1-b550-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-100138-100414-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d75e6228-a907-11f1-b550-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-100138-100414-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">61d66626-a90d-11f1-9655-456b2dea8570</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 10:16:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d75e6228-a907-11f1-b550-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-100138-100414-CS.jpg">© FRANCE 24 screen capture</source><dc:creator>Shahzaib WAHLAH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>Himalayan hydropower buildout: Expert says risk management is key</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20260904-rebuilding-after-nepal-flash-floods-expert-says-risk-management-is-key-in-himalayas</link><description>
Following devastating floods in Nepal and Tibet, Access Asia takes a closer look at the fragile state of the Himalayan mountains. Dr Arun Bhakta Shrestha, an expert on the environment and risk management in the Himalayas, explains why it's so difficult to detect glacier movements in advance and says that the tragedy could serve as an opportunity to improve the way nations develop infrastructure in the resource-rich region. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fb9cb7c-a866-11f1-947a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/nepal-flooding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fb9cb7c-a866-11f1-947a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/nepal-flooding.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9710a5ce-a85c-11f1-994b-6be82c255321</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 14:34:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal floods: Two workers pulled alive from tunnel after nine days</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-floods-two-workers-pulled-alive-from-tunnel-after-nine-days</link><description>
Nepal's emergency crews have pulled two workers out of a hydropower tunnel where they had been trapped for nine days. The rescue comes more than a week after flash flooding along the Nepal-Tibet border killed more than 1,200 people. Both men have injuries to their hands and legs and have been airlifted to a hospital in Kathmandu for treatment.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/334b72d4-a862-11f1-b1e7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12044774156a9ac39a0f8209-45355415.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/334b72d4-a862-11f1-b1e7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12044774156a9ac39a0f8209-45355415.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c8ee8822-a85c-11f1-b433-ef8cb436237b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 13:54:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Two trapped workers rescued from mud-clogged tunnel 9 days after Nepal floods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-two-trapped-workers-rescued-from-mud-clogged-tunnel-9-days-after-nepal-floods</link><description>
Nine days after catastrophic floods hit Nepal, hope emerges from the dark as two workers have been rescued from a collapsed tunnel. They are receiving treatment as emergency crews race to find more survivors. The floods killed more than 1,200 people and left over 5,000 missing. An estimated 115 people are still believed trapped in the tunnel.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8f330d4-a81b-11f1-bc29-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247155624727.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8f330d4-a81b-11f1-bc29-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247155624727.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c3557f3e-a83d-11f1-8c5d-7560b05da2a5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 10:12:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>#Nepal: Two flood survivors rescued from hydropower tunnel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-two-flood-survivors-rescued-from-hydropower-tunnel</link><description>
In a video posted to social media on September 4, the Nepali #army announced it had rescued two workers trapped in a hydropower tunnel. The rescue brings hope of reaching over a dozen others thought to be trapped inside the tunnel. Both men were flown to a hospital in #Kathmandu. The floods killed more than 1,200 people, and over 5,000 are still missing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3db53ed6-a843-11f1-b910-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Vignette-Nepal-rescue-tunnels.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3db53ed6-a843-11f1-b910-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Vignette-Nepal-rescue-tunnels.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5119e936-a843-11f1-bb54-e71901705b94</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 09:38:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Why early warning signs of glacier collapse in Nepal were difficult to detect</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-nepal-why-early-warning-signs-of-glacier-collapse-were-difficult-to-detect</link><description>
The glacier collapse that led to devastating flash floods across the Himalayan region of Nepal and its border with the Chinese autonomous region of Tibet on August 26 was preceded by early warning signs, experts say. But monitoring and emergency alert systems in the region are still insufficient to predict such disasters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37302d74-a7b1-11f1-b839-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242130815701.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37302d74-a7b1-11f1-b839-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242130815701.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6e4aea6-a7b8-11f1-86d1-df5f1bac4863</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 07:24:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37302d74-a7b1-11f1-b839-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242130815701.jpg">© Rajesh Kumar Singh, AP</source><dc:creator>Simon FEISTHAUER FOURNET</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>USS Lincoln crew hits the streets of Thailand's Pattaya after nine-month deployment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-uss-lincoln-crew-hits-the-streets-of-thailand-pattaya-after-nine-month-deployment</link><description>
US sailors and Marines streamed into the Thai resort city of Pattaya Thursday after a record-breaking nine months at sea. Local police said there had so far been no major incidents connected to the 5,000-strong contingent of US service members, though two sailors were sent back to the ship after a drunken bar brawl.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc92066-a829-11f1-87f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T151123Z-151811266-RC2MBNAFAEVC-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-THAILAND-USA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc92066-a829-11f1-87f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T151123Z-151811266-RC2MBNAFAEVC-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-THAILAND-USA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">36c85f46-a829-11f1-ac16-dbecab1efb8a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 07:02:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc92066-a829-11f1-87f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T151123Z-151811266-RC2MBNAFAEVC-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-THAILAND-USA.jpg">© Chalinee Thirasupa, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Two trapped hydropower workers rescued from mud-clogged tunnel in Nepal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-two-trapped-hydropower-workers-rescued-from-mud-clogged-tunnel-in-nepal</link><description>
Rescue teams on Friday pulled two hydropower workers free from a tunnel blocked by mud and debris during the massive flood that swept through Nepal in late August. Officials believe that hundreds of workers remain trapped in tunnels connected to hydropower projects throughout the remote Himalayan region.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8f330d4-a81b-11f1-bc29-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247155624727.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8f330d4-a81b-11f1-bc29-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247155624727.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9890d3e2-a81b-11f1-8947-29ab28e6c15a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 05:10:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8f330d4-a81b-11f1-bc29-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247155624727.jpg">Nepal Army via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>‘Fight through darkness, water’: Nepal survivor recounts escape from flood-hit tunnel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260903-fight-through-darkness-water-nepal-survivor-recounts-escape-from-flood-hit-tunnel</link><description>
A Nepalese worker recounts his harrowing escape from a hydropower project tunnel after last week's devastating flood. Around 900 workers remain trapped in tunnels at six hydroelectric plants in Nepal as the number of missing in the Himalayan disaster rose to 5,624 on Thursday, according to Nepalese and Chinese authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c0b6cb6-a7b0-11f1-962a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T141836Z-1431816270-RC2FBNAICU0M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-TUNNEL-SURVIVOR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c0b6cb6-a7b0-11f1-962a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T141836Z-1431816270-RC2FBNAICU0M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-TUNNEL-SURVIVOR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38461b4c-a7b1-11f1-952d-dd80a2f2ae2e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 17:22:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c0b6cb6-a7b0-11f1-962a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T141836Z-1431816270-RC2FBNAICU0M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-TUNNEL-SURVIVOR.jpg">© Joseph Campbell, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal: How are the hundreds of victims from the floods being identified?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-how-are-the-hundreds-of-victims-from-the-floods-being-identified</link><description>
#Nepal faces a major challenge: identifying the remains that have been found after the #flood that tore through part of the country on August 26, some of which are in an advanced state of decomposition. For #health reasons, the unidentified bodies have begun to be buried. Before each #burial, #DNA samples are taken and an identification number is assigned to each set of remains. Relatives of those reported missing can visit DNA collection centres to provide a sample. Their genetic profile can then be compared with that of the bodies found, in the hope of identifying them. FRANCE 24’s correspondents visited one such centre, set up within the #police #hospital in #Kathmandu.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14e0b356-a784-11f1-8616-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-DNA-2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14e0b356-a784-11f1-8616-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-DNA-2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">372b7b3a-a784-11f1-b089-bba181e6f0ff</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:52:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>After Nepal’s devastating floods, DNA tests help identify victims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-struggles-to-identify-the-remains-found-in-floods</link><description>
The recent flash floods in Nepal have left authorities facing a major challenge: identifying the remains that have been recovered, some of which are in an advanced state of decomposition. For health reasons, unidentified bodies have begun to be buried. Before each burial, DNA samples are taken, while relatives of people reported missing can visit DNA collection centres to provide samples of their own. Their genetic profiles can then be compared with those of the recovered remains, in the hope of identifying them. FRANCE 24’s team on the ground reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0565c404-a773-11f1-b000-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245531226042.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0565c404-a773-11f1-b000-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245531226042.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a137a40-a774-11f1-b2c5-4168adfd404e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:06:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Philippine couple married in hip-deep floodwaters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-philippine-couple-married-in-hip-deep-floodwaters</link><description>
A Philippine couple tied the knot on Tuesday at a Catholic church swamped in hip-deep waters, as heavy rains had pummelled large parts of the country for a month.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7030a242-a6e0-11f1-80ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7030a242-a6e0-11f1-80ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84ba1356-a6e0-11f1-802a-c1762cef3722</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 15:21:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>FRANCE 24 in Nepal: The unbearable wait for missing relatives</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-france-24-in-nepal-the-unbearable-wait-for-missing-relatives</link><description>
In Nepal, the hope of finding survivors is fading daily. Bodies are piling up in morgues, and storage capacity is reaching its limit. For the relatives of the missing, the wait is unbearable. They go from one hospital to another, consult the lists of survivors and scrutinise the photos of unidentified bodies. FRANCE 24's special correspondents met with several of these families at the morgue of Kathmandu University Hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f3774cc-a6d4-11f1-9f06-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f3774cc-a6d4-11f1-9f06-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">971a982e-a6d4-11f1-9051-c3a5f90ffaca</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:03:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>FRANCE 24 in Nepal: In Bharatpur, authorities begin burying unidentified bodies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-france-24-in-nepal-in-bharatpur-authorities-begin-burying-unidentified-bodies</link><description>
In Nepal, the death toll continues to rise. Every day, new bodies are recovered, but many remain unidentifiable. Several days after the devastating floods, some are already in an advanced state of decomposition. Faced with the influx of remains, authorities have begun burying them without formal identification, primarily to limit health risks and the strong odours. FRANCE 24's special correspondents traveled to Bharatpur, in southern Nepal, to one of these burial sites.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f1bfadc-a6b7-11f1-829a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f1bfadc-a6b7-11f1-829a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d25e53b6-a6b7-11f1-b43e-c7c8f9905ae8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 10:28:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Nepal tunnel rescuers hit dead ends as search for trapped workers continues</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260902-nepal-tunnel-rescuers-hit-dead-ends-as-they-search-for-trapped-workers</link><description>
Rescue teams in Nepal were still searching Wednesday for hundreds of workers believed to have been trapped inside sprawling hydropower tunnels since the catastrophic flash flood that swept through the Himalayan region last week. Officials said that many of the tunnels remain totally blocked by mud and debris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07368da2-a577-11f1-849f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/fe0cc43fd6df4a151e4418359eb746514777f1dd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07368da2-a577-11f1-849f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/fe0cc43fd6df4a151e4418359eb746514777f1dd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a265e8e-a69e-11f1-b6d9-bbaab86a6a73</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 07:15:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07368da2-a577-11f1-849f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/fe0cc43fd6df4a151e4418359eb746514777f1dd.jpg">© Nepal Army handout via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong pleads guilty to foreign collusion</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260902-hong-kong-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-pleads-guilty-to-foreign-collusion</link><description>
Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong on Wednesday pleaded guilty to colluding with foreign powers in a trial that could see the 29-year-old spend the rest of his life behind bars. Wong rose to international prominence for his involvement in the 2014 Umbrella Movement and the mass protests against Beijing that rocked the financial hub in 2019.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1394dca-a67d-11f1-8d13-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/a1aae207cc66eb9e2a6f4da70d7892c1c97dfc9f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1394dca-a67d-11f1-8d13-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/a1aae207cc66eb9e2a6f4da70d7892c1c97dfc9f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a28eb0c0-a67d-11f1-9782-7dc4763c3d39</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 03:23:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1394dca-a67d-11f1-8d13-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/a1aae207cc66eb9e2a6f4da70d7892c1c97dfc9f.jpg">© Vivek Prakash, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>USS Lincoln carrier docks near Thailand's Pattaya resort after nine months at sea</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260902-uss-abraham-lincoln-aircraft-carrier-docks-in-thailand-after-nine-months-at-sea</link><description>
More than 5,000 US sailors and Marines arrived in Thailand Wednesday after nine months at sea on the USS Abraham Lincoln aircraft carrier. The carrier's long deployment in the Middle East during the US-Israeli war on Iran sparked reports of worsening mental health crises on board, including attempted suicides.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33e97066-a677-11f1-8743-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/062f36e998a80c16df9801843c77d0110baa0656.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33e97066-a677-11f1-8743-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/062f36e998a80c16df9801843c77d0110baa0656.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34d96e2c-a677-11f1-b4e8-d939bff7b5e4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 02:37:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33e97066-a677-11f1-8743-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/062f36e998a80c16df9801843c77d0110baa0656.jpg">© Anthony Wallace, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mass burials held in Nepal as bodies wash up after catastrophic flooding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/mass-burials-held-in-nepal-as-bodies-wash-up-after-catastrophic-flooding</link><description>
Every day, new bodies are recovered in Nepal, but many remain unidentifiable. Several days after the disaster, some are already in an advanced state of decomposition. Morgues in the country's main cities are reaching capacity. Faced with the influx of remains, authorities have begun burying them without formal identification. France 24's special correspondents traveled to Bharatpur, in southern Nepal, to one of these burial sites.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f70db168-a633-11f1-8dfc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260901-200150-200343-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f70db168-a633-11f1-8dfc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260901-200150-200343-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fca13ff0-a633-11f1-a97d-af91c05e98b9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 18:40:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>After the floods, Nepal works to bury hundreds of washed-up unidentified bodies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-works-to-bury-hundreds-of-washed-up-unidentified-bodies</link><description>
Nepal is burying dozens of bodies in multiple trenches as Nepal’s disaster agency said that 1,003 deaths had been counted there, with 3,916 people missing, including 583 foreign nationals. In its latest update, China reported 16 deaths and 546 missing, including 261 foreigners. Crews faced challenging conditions as they searched unstable terrain and piles of debris. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a7435174-a476-11f1-ad38-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-30T132655Z-836715202-RC209NA6ORCP-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-MASSBURIAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a7435174-a476-11f1-ad38-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-30T132655Z-836715202-RC209NA6ORCP-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-MASSBURIAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f853d4b2-a606-11f1-aceb-77a48fff9120</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:08:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal's rescuers navigate mud-swamped tunnels for hundreds of missing workers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-s-rescuers-navigate-mud-swamped-tunnels-for-hundreds-of-missing-workers</link><description>
The death toll in Nepal has crossed 1,000 from the deadly floods that tore through an area on the border with Tibet on August 26, and nearly 4,000 people remain missing. six days on hopes for survivors are dimming, but rescuers focused on a network of hydropower sites along the Trishuli River are holding out hope. Of the roughly 900 workers missing, some 500 people are believed to be trapped in the tunnels, according to Nepalese authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f37cc1f0-a517-11f1-b844-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VW7CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f37cc1f0-a517-11f1-b844-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VW7CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">04b62fcc-a605-11f1-863b-f9580e1f490b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:59:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
